480e0955 (2743 1792789426491 "guenchi" (("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing f321a") (src . "store: a writer belongs to the instance its owner names; the local writer is chosen by ownership, not by name order\n\nA writer directory copied in from another checkout sorted first and was taken\nas the local writer: writes went into another instance's log, and the copy\nanswered `(instance nonce)` on its own writes. Now:\n\n- A writer is this instance's when its `owner.sexp` names the `(machine\n  nonce)` this copy's `instance.sexp` records. Every choice of the writer to\n  extend (a write's, `position`'s, a commit's cursor, `adopt`'s own) prefers\n  such a writer and passes over a live one whose owner names another instance\n  or carries no instance field. A writer whose owner cannot be read is not\n  passed over: it stays where it is and its write is refused\n  `owner-unreadable`. When no live writer names this instance, the first local\n  writer in name order is chosen, as before.\n- `instance.sexp` is metadata the session watches: a request whose writer\n  comes to be passed over while it runs is refused `(writer-superseded (writer\n  <w>) (by <o>) (remedy reopen))`, and the next request writes as `<o>`; an\n  append after a rewrite of the file is refused for its epoch before anything\n  rotates.\n- The paths that change drafts (`write`, `restore`, `discard` of a draft that\n  is there, `commit`, the structural drafts a landing tool writes) refuse a\n  `--writer` whose owner names another instance: `(error foreign-writer\n  (writer <w>) (remedy draft-writer))`. A session draft writer has no owner\n  and is accepted as before; reading such a draft, the replay of a tracked\n  commit and the completion of a persisted plan are answered as before.\n- `check` reports whose writers the store holds, without changing the\n  verdict: `writer-owner-foreign`, `writer-owner-unverified`,\n  `instance-absent (remedy adopt)`, `instance-unavailable`; a retired writer is\n  not listed; when the local writer's log cannot be read it is listed\n  `unreadable` and no foreign writer is named in its place.\n- `retire!` and the discard of an absent draft keep their refusals under the\n  ownership gate; the owner nonce is compared as a datum.\n- Rows in test/ownership.sc (159); append-prefix's rotation scenario follows\n  the watched file; `ownership` is a fault domain of its own (the table's\n  reads of instance.sexp and each writer's owner and retirement); README\n  sections for the local writer, drafts, `check` and `adopt`.\n") (parent . root) (ord . 460))))
